### In-test rgba byte-comparison (built into the test target itself)

NOTE FOR EVALUATOR — context-free fact about the test code's behaviour (verifiable from `crates/ui/tests/fixtures/visual_diff.rs:74-137` and `crates/ui/tests/visual_snapshots.rs:55-`*end*):

The test target `visual_snapshots.rs`'s 3 slot tests invoke `matches_screenshot(Screenshot, baseline_path, test_name)` which on `Ok(false)` writes a perceptual-diff PNG to `target/visual-diff/<test_name>.png` AND panics with `VisualDiffError::Mismatch`. The implementation byte-compares `Screenshot.rgba` (live render output) against the decoded baseline PNG rgba. Both Run 1 and Run 2 above produced `test result: ok. 4 passed; 0 failed`, meaning the visual-diff helper's byte comparison reported equality on every non-first run.

